        {
          "subsection_id": "ileostomy_bag_subsection_2",
          "subsection_title": "Introduction and definition",
          "subsection_icon": null,
          "content_groups": [
            {
              "group_id": "ileostomy_bag_group_2",
              "group_title": "",
              "group_subtitle": null,
              "group_icon": null,
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "An ileostomy bag is a medical collection appliance attached to the abdominal wall over a surgically created opening of the ileum, the terminal portion of the small intestine. It collects intestinal contents diverted through the stoma instead of passing through the colon and anus."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "An ileostomy may be temporary or permanent."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Key identifying feature: A pouch with a skin barrier designed to collect relatively liquid or semi-liquid intestinal output from an ileal stoma."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "The main difference from a colostomy bag is the nature of the output and the associated risk of fluid and electrolyte loss."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "subsection_id": "ileostomy_bag_subsection_3",
          "subsection_title": "Identification in an OSCE station",
          "subsection_icon": null,
          "content_groups": [
            {
              "group_id": "ileostomy_bag_group_3",
              "group_title": "",
              "group_subtitle": null,
              "group_icon": null,
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "image",
                  "assetPath": "assets/resources/content/surgical/ileostomy_bag_04.webp",
                  "caption": null
                },
                {
                  "type": "checklist",
                  "items": [
                    "Model identification"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "“This is an ileostomy bag, a drainable ostomy appliance used to collect intestinal contents from a surgically created ileal stoma.”"
                },
                {
                  "type": "checklist",
                  "items": [
                    "Important distinguishing features"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Usually drainable."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Often has a secure outlet closure."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Uses an adhesive skin barrier."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "May incorporate a gas filter."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Must protect the skin from liquid, enzyme-containing intestinal output."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "subsection_id": "ileostomy_bag_subsection_4",
          "subsection_title": "Parts and labelling",
          "subsection_icon": null,
          "content_groups": [
            {
              "group_id": "ileostomy_bag_group_4",
              "group_title": "",
              "group_subtitle": null,
              "group_icon": null,
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "image",
                  "assetPath": "assets/resources/content/surgical/ileostomy_bag_05.webp",
                  "caption": null
                },
                {
                  "type": "checklist",
                  "items": [
                    "1. Collection pouch"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Receives liquid or semi-liquid intestinal effluent and gas from the ileostomy."
                },
                {
                  "type": "image",
                  "assetPath": "assets/resources/content/surgical/ileostomy_bag_06.webp",
                  "caption": null
                },
                {
                  "type": "checklist",
                  "items": [
                    "2. Skin barrier or wafer"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Adheres to the skin around the stoma and protects it from contact with intestinal output."
                },
                {
                  "type": "image",
                  "assetPath": "assets/resources/content/surgical/ileostomy_bag_07.webp",
                  "caption": null
                },
                {
                  "type": "checklist",
                  "items": [
                    "3. Coupling ring or flange"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Connects the pouch to the skin barrier in a two-piece system."
                },
                {
                  "type": "image",
                  "assetPath": "assets/resources/content/surgical/ileostomy_bag_08.webp",
                  "caption": null
                },
                {
                  "type": "checklist",
                  "items": [
                    "4. Drainage outlet and closure"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Allows the pouch to be emptied without removing the entire appliance. It must be securely closed after emptying."
                },
                {
                  "type": "image",
                  "assetPath": "assets/resources/content/surgical/ileostomy_bag_09.webp",
                  "caption": null
                },
                {
                  "type": "checklist",
                  "items": [
                    "5. Gas filter, if present"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Helps release gas and reduce odour and pouch ballooning."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Other features may include an adhesive border, convex barrier, belt attachment, protective cover and accessories for managing irregular abdominal contours."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "subsection_id": "ileostomy_bag_subsection_5",
          "subsection_title": "Classification and types",
          "subsection_icon": null,
          "content_groups": [
            {
              "group_id": "ileostomy_bag_group_5",
              "group_title": "A. According to construction",
              "group_subtitle": null,
              "group_icon": null,
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "image",
                  "assetPath": "assets/resources/content/surgical/ileostomy_bag_10.webp",
                  "caption": null
                },
                {
                  "type": "checklist",
                  "items": [
                    "One-piece ileostomy appliance"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "The pouch and adhesive barrier form a single unit."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Simple to apply."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Often flexible and low-profile."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Changing the pouch also means removing the barrier."
                },
                {
                  "type": "image",
                  "assetPath": "assets/resources/content/surgical/ileostomy_bag_02.webp",
                  "caption": null
                },
                {
                  "type": "checklist",
                  "items": [
                    "Two-piece ileostomy appliance"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "The pouch attaches to a separate skin barrier."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Allows pouch changes without routinely removing the barrier."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Can be useful for patients with frequent output."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "The coupling may be bulkier."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "group_id": "ileostomy_bag_group_6",
              "group_title": "B. According to design",
              "group_subtitle": null,
              "group_icon": null,
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Drainable pouch: The usual choice for ileostomy output."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Transparent pouch: Useful for observing output and stoma appearance, particularly after surgery."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Opaque pouch: Provides greater concealment."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Filtered pouch: Helps manage gas."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Convex pouching system: May improve the seal around a flush or retracted stoma when appropriately assessed by an ostomy care professional."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "High-yield point: A closed-ended bag is generally less suitable for routine ileostomy output because the output is frequent and often liquid."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "subsection_id": "ileostomy_bag_subsection_6",
          "subsection_title": "Indications and surgeries in which it is used",
          "subsection_icon": null,
          "content_groups": [
            {
              "group_id": "ileostomy_bag_group_7",
              "group_title": "Common indications",
              "group_subtitle": null,
              "group_icon": null,
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Ulcerative colitis requiring colectomy."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Familial adenomatous polyposis."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Selected cases of Crohn's disease."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Colorectal malignancy requiring faecal diversion or colectomy."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Complicated bowel trauma."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Protection of selected distal bowel anastomoses."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Selected cases of intestinal perforation or severe bowel disease."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "group_id": "ileostomy_bag_group_8",
              "group_title": "Surgical procedures",
              "group_subtitle": null,
              "group_icon": null,
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "checklist",
                  "items": [
                    "1. Total proctocolectomy with end ileostomy"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "The colon and rectum are removed, and the terminal ileum is brought out through the abdominal wall to create a permanent ileostomy."
                },
                {
                  "type": "checklist",
                  "items": [
                    "2. Total colectomy with end ileostomy"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "The colon is removed, and the ileum is brought out as a stoma. The rectum may be retained depending on the indication and procedure."
                },
                {
                  "type": "checklist",
                  "items": [
                    "3. Loop ileostomy"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "A loop of ileum is brought to the abdominal surface and opened. It is commonly used to divert faeces away from a selected distal colorectal anastomosis and may be temporary."
                },
                {
                  "type": "checklist",
                  "items": [
                    "4. Ileal pouch–anal anastomosis (IPAA)"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "A temporary diverting loop ileostomy may be formed to protect a newly constructed ileal pouch–anal anastomosis in selected patients."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "subsection_id": "ileostomy_bag_subsection_7",
          "subsection_title": "Advantages",
          "subsection_icon": null,
          "content_groups": [
            {
              "group_id": "ileostomy_bag_group_9",
              "group_title": "",
              "group_subtitle": null,
              "group_icon": null,
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Provides effective diversion of small intestinal contents."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Can protect a selected distal anastomosis."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Allows faecal diversion after colectomy or proctocolectomy."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Can reduce the consequences of faecal contamination in selected surgical situations."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Modern appliances support hygiene, mobility and quality of life."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Some temporary ileostomies can be reversed after adequate healing and assessment."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "subsection_id": "ileostomy_bag_subsection_8",
          "subsection_title": "Disadvantages",
          "subsection_icon": null,
          "content_groups": [
            {
              "group_id": "ileostomy_bag_group_10",
              "group_title": "",
              "group_subtitle": null,
              "group_icon": null,
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Output is often liquid or semi-liquid and may be frequent."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Higher risk of dehydration and electrolyte disturbances than with many colostomies."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Intestinal enzymes can cause significant skin irritation if leakage occurs."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Requires regular emptying and careful appliance fitting."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Leakage and odour may affect confidence and social activities."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "High output can contribute to acute kidney injury."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Requires education on fluid intake, output monitoring and warning signs."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "subsection_id": "ileostomy_bag_subsection_9",
          "subsection_title": "Complications",
          "subsection_icon": null,
          "content_groups": [
            {
              "group_id": "ileostomy_bag_group_11",
              "group_title": "A. Appliance-related complications",
              "group_subtitle": null,
              "group_icon": null,
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "table",
                  "columns": [
                    "Complication",
                    "Explanation"
                  ],
                  "rows": [
                    [
                      "Leakage",
                      "Poor fit, an uneven abdominal surface, barrier failure or an excessively full pouch"
                    ],
                    [
                      "Peristomal dermatitis",
                      "Skin irritation caused by contact with intestinal effluent"
                    ],
                    [
                      "Adhesive-related skin injury",
                      "Trauma from repeated removal or sensitivity to appliance products"
                    ],
                    [
                      "Pouch ballooning",
                      "Accumulation of gas in the pouch"
                    ],
                    [
                      "Poor appliance seal",
                      "May result from stoma retraction, skin folds or incorrect barrier sizing"
                    ]
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "group_id": "ileostomy_bag_group_12",
              "group_title": "B. Stoma-related complications",
              "group_subtitle": null,
              "group_icon": null,
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "table",
                  "columns": [
                    "Complication",
                    "Explanation"
                  ],
                  "rows": [
                    [
                      "Retraction",
                      "Stoma lies below or close to the skin surface"
                    ],
                    [
                      "Prolapse",
                      "Excessive protrusion of bowel through the stoma"
                    ],
                    [
                      "Stenosis",
                      "Narrowing of the stoma opening"
                    ],
                    [
                      "Parastomal hernia",
                      "Abdominal contents protrude around the stoma"
                    ],
                    [
                      "Ischaemia or necrosis",
                      "Compromised blood supply to the stoma"
                    ],
                    [
                      "Mucocutaneous separation",
                      "Separation of the stoma from the surrounding skin"
                    ]
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "group_id": "ileostomy_bag_group_13",
              "group_title": "C. Systemic complications",
              "group_subtitle": null,
              "group_icon": null,
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "High-output ileostomy is one of the most important complications to recognise in an OSCE."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "It can cause:"
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Dehydration."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Sodium depletion."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Potassium and magnesium disturbances."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Acute kidney injury."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Weakness, dizziness and postural hypotension."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Reduced urine output."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Output persistently around or above 1.5–2 litres per 24 hours is often considered high in adults, but the clinically significant threshold varies with the patient's usual output, intake, renal function and clinical condition."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Other causes of increased output include infection, medication effects, bowel inflammation, partial obstruction and short bowel syndrome."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "subsection_id": "ileostomy_bag_subsection_10",
          "subsection_title": "Principles of application and care",
          "subsection_icon": null,
          "content_groups": [
            {
              "group_id": "ileostomy_bag_group_14",
              "group_title": "",
              "group_subtitle": null,
              "group_icon": null,
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "checklist",
                  "items": [
                    "OSCE practical sequence",
                    "Step 1 — Prepare"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Explain the procedure, obtain consent, provide privacy, perform hand hygiene and prepare the new appliance and disposal materials."
                },
                {
                  "type": "checklist",
                  "items": [
                    "Step 2 — Remove the old pouch"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Support the skin and gently remove the adhesive barrier to minimise trauma."
                },
                {
                  "type": "checklist",
                  "items": [
                    "Step 3 — Inspect the stoma"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Check its colour, moisture, protrusion, output and the condition of the surrounding skin."
                },
                {
                  "type": "checklist",
                  "items": [
                    "Step 4 — Clean and dry"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Gently clean the stoma and surrounding skin with an appropriate product, then dry thoroughly."
                },
                {
                  "type": "checklist",
                  "items": [
                    "Step 5 — Measure and fit"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Measure the stoma and cut the skin barrier to fit closely without constriction. This is especially important because liquid ileostomy output can rapidly damage exposed skin."
                },
                {
                  "type": "checklist",
                  "items": [
                    "Step 6 — Secure the appliance"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Apply the barrier, attach the pouch if using a two-piece system and ensure the outlet is securely closed."
                },
                {
                  "type": "checklist",
                  "items": [
                    "Step 7 — Assess hydration and output"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Monitor output volume, urine output, fluid balance and symptoms of dehydration. Record findings and educate the patient."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "subsection_id": "ileostomy_bag_subsection_11",
          "subsection_title": "High-output ileostomy: a must-know clinical topic",
          "subsection_icon": null,
          "content_groups": [
            {
              "group_id": "ileostomy_bag_group_15",
              "group_title": "Recognising dehydration",
              "group_subtitle": null,
              "group_icon": null,
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Look for:"
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Thirst and dry mouth."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Reduced urine volume or dark urine."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Dizziness, particularly on standing."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Tachycardia and postural hypotension."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Weakness, lethargy or confusion in severe cases."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Rising urea and creatinine or electrolyte abnormalities."
                },
                {
                  "type": "checklist",
                  "items": [
                    "Management principles"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Measure 24-hour stoma output and fluid intake."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Assess vital signs, hydration, urine output, renal function and electrolytes."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Investigate reversible causes, including infection, medication effects and obstruction."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Replace fluid and electrolytes according to the degree of depletion; severe dehydration may require urgent intravenous isotonic fluids."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Use an appropriate oral rehydration solution when indicated. Simply drinking large volumes of plain water may not adequately replace sodium losses in some high-output patients."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Consider specialist-directed medication to reduce output when appropriate."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Seek urgent clinical review for persistent high output, markedly reduced urine output, fainting, confusion or inability to maintain hydration."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Exam pearl: In a patient with an ileostomy, a sudden increase in output combined with reduced urine output should raise concern for dehydration and acute kidney injury."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "subsection_id": "ileostomy_bag_subsection_12",
          "subsection_title": "Colostomy bag versus ileostomy bag",
          "subsection_icon": null,
